    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the roster as our undisputed offensive engine. With a score of 81.88, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a premium leadoff spot against the hittable Alcantara, where his dynamic platoon advantage creates an ideal environment for production across all five categories. Following closely is **Josh Lowe**, who, despite being buried in the order at #9, offers a high-upside play (71.68) against the struggling Erick Fedde. **Josh Lowe** is specifically targeted for his elite sprint speed and a high-probability stolen base opportunity against a slow-delivering pitcher, effectively mitigating the penalty of his bottom-order placement. Both **Nolan Schanuel** and **Josh Jung** also project as high-floor starters, with the latter capitalizing on a massive 7.06 xERA matchup against E-Rod, providing significant value for a UTIL slot.\n\nStrategic deployment today heavily favors players facing favorable wind conditions and soft opposing rotations. **Miguel Vargas** and **Sam Antonacci** are currently pending official lineup confirmation, but should they hit in the top third of the order as expected, they become potent options against Aldegheri. **Sam Antonacci**, in particular, remains a high-variance target; despite a minor platoon disadvantage, his elite 0.404 xwOBA makes him a core play. Conversely, **Kyle Tucker** (58.53) sits just inside our start threshold; while his raw talent is superior, the matchup against Lambert offers less path-to-ceiling than our other outfield options today.\n\nThe most difficult call on the bench involves **Marcell Ozuna**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 59.97 score. While **Marcell Ozuna** carries significant power, the optimizer favored the efficiency and speed profiles of **Heliot Ramos** and **Josh Lowe** to maximize our output in the steals category\u2014our most critical scarcity. We are maintaining a cautious approach regarding **Jackson Merrill** and the aforementioned pending lineups, as the projected matchup against a crafty arm like Webb introduces enough volatility to monitor closely before first pitch. We will avoid overextending our game caps on lower-efficiency bench bats like **Andy Pages** and **Coby Mayo** until deeper in the week, preferring to prioritize the high-efficiency, speed-oriented core currently in place.",
